@segment 54-56 Winterspring
@start-level 54
# Dwarf, any class (made from the Gnome route by tools/derive_anyclass.py). From the Dwarf route's segment 22: same quests, order, binds and flights. This segment had no class
# quests and no second-hearthstone step, so no travel changed: the last step is the ordinary Hearthstone to Everlook
# (unused since the start of the segment). Only the combat hints and the bind / hearth texts were rewritten class-neutral.
# Winterfall Totemic and Winterfall Shaman are mob names (quest targets of 5082 and 8464).
# Carried in from segment 21: The New Springs (980) and It's a Secret to Everybody (3908) for Donova Snowden,
# To Winterspring! (5249) for Wynd Nightchaser and Speak to Salfa (8465).
@carry 980,3908,5249,8465
# Prerequisites of the carried quests (3845 -> 3908, 974 -> 980 in segment 20; 8461 -> 8465 in segment 21).
@done 3845,974,8461
# Order: Timbermaw Hold -> Salfa and Donova -> the western Winterfall camps (the firewater flask drops there) -> Donova's
# firewater chain with two short trips back through the tunnel into Felwood -> grind to 55 -> Starfall Village ->
# Everlook (bind) -> yetis and Winterfall Village with the grind to 56 -> Starfall, Lake Kel'Theril, the wrecked camp
# and Darkwhisper Gorge in the south -> back west for Donova's last quests and Salfa -> hearth to Everlook.
# Hearth: Astranaar until Everlook, then Everlook.
# Changes against the plan, all inside this segment:
# - The grind is split: L 55 on the level 53-56 furbolgs in the west first, L 56 at Winterfall Village before the
#   level 56-59 yetis and owlbeasts. Everything east of Starfall is 55-59, too high for a fresh 54.
# - Threat of the Winterfall (5082) needs Trouble in Winterspring! (6603) from Everlook, so it is done on the way back
#   west at the end, together with the hand-ins of 4842 and 8464.
# - The Final Piece (5123) is left out: its log only drops from High Chief Winterfall, an elite.
# - Are We There, Yeti? part 3 (5163) is not taken: its hand-in needs a flight to Gadgetzan and Un'Goro and a trip back
#   to Everlook, and the route leaves Winterspring for good at the end of this segment.
# - Toxic Horrors (5086) can only be taken after Mystery Goo (5085) is handed to Donova: two trips into Felwood, not one.
# Skipped as planned: 3909 (Feralas), 5121 (elite), 5128 (Felwood), 4808-4810, the Darnassus and Moonglade chains.
# Carry-out (3): 5245, 6028, 6030.

# ---------- The tunnel exit: Salfa and Donova ----------
G Winterspring, 27.7, 34.5 | You start at Nafien at level 54, hearthstone set to Astranaar. Walk through Timbermaw Hold and keep right for the Winterspring exit. Never attack the Timbermaw furbolgs inside
T 8465 | Salfa, at the tunnel exit
A 8464 | Salfa. Den Watchers live in the camps right here; Shamans and Ursa only in Winterfall Village, far to the east
T 3908 | Donova Snowden, beside the hot springs a short ride south-east. She offers The Videre Elixir next: skip it, it is a Feralas trip
T 980 | Donova Snowden
A 4842 | Donova Snowden. The spot is in the far south of Winterspring: you go there from Everlook

# ---------- Western Winterfall camps: the firewater chain and the grind to 55 ----------
N Kill Winterfall furbolgs in the camp just south-east of Salfa until one drops an Empty Firewater Flask @ Winterspring, 31.5, 36.3 | The camp spreads over 30-34, 35-37: Pathfinders (53-54), Totemics (54-55) and three Den Watchers (55-56, they count for Salfa). About 1 kill in 10 drops the flask. A Totemic sets down totems: kill those first. Pull one at a time from the edge of the camp and eat or bandage between pulls. Salfa buys Winterfall Spirit Beads 5 at a time: loot everything
A 5083 @ Winterspring, 31.5, 36.3 | Right-click the Empty Firewater Flask. No flask after 30 kills or so? Go on to the grind step below and take it when it drops; without it, skip Donova's chain
T 5083 | Donova Snowden
A 5084 | Donova Snowden
N Go back through Timbermaw Hold to the Felwood side | Short trip number one. Carrying 5 Winterfall Spirit Beads? Hand them to Salfa as you pass
T 5084 @ Felwood, 60.2, 5.8 | The Deadwood Cauldron in the middle of Felpaw Village, just west of Nafien. Clear the furbolgs around it first
A 5085 @ Felwood, 60.2, 5.8 | The Deadwood Cauldron
T 5085 | Back through the tunnel to Donova Snowden
A 5086 | Donova Snowden
N Go back through Timbermaw Hold once more | Short trip number two
C 5086 @ Felwood, 49.7, 25.0 | Irontree Woods, down the road south-west of Felpaw Village: Toxic Horrors (53-54) drop the 3 droplets, nearly every kill. They poison: cure it if your class can, otherwise bandage and eat
T 5086 | Back through the tunnel to Donova Snowden
A 5087 | Donova Snowden. The runners are level 57 and come three at a time: grind first
L 55 @ Winterspring, 31.5, 36.3 | Quest XP is thin in Winterspring. Grind the two Winterfall camps in the west to 55: the big one south-east of Salfa (30-34, 35-37) and the one east of Donova (39-42, 42-45). Every kill adds Timbermaw reputation, and the Den Watchers count for Salfa (three in the first camp, one in the second). Pull singles from the edge and get back to full health between pulls
C 5087 @ Winterspring, 27.9, 34.5 | Three Winterfall Runners (57) come out of the Timbermaw tunnel beside Salfa and walk east along the road toward Winterfall Village. Wait at the exit, or ride the road east until you meet them. They come as a group of three: start at full health with your cooldowns ready (if you have a pet, send it first), slow or disable the others if your class can, kill them one by one and loot the Winterfall Crate. Going badly? Run back toward Salfa and try again
T 5087 | Donova Snowden. Skip High Chief Winterfall: he is elite

# ---------- Starfall Village and Everlook ----------
T 5249 | Ride east along the road to Starfall Village, the night elf lodge on the hill north of Lake Kel'Theril. Wynd Nightchaser is inside
A 5244 | Wynd Nightchaser
T 5244 | Jaron Stoneshaper, the dwarf standing next to her
A 5245 | Jaron gives you his pick. The fragments are in the lake south of here; you collect them after Everlook
G Winterspring, 61.0, 38.0 | Ride on east to Everlook
F Everlook @ Winterspring, 62.3, 36.6 | Maethrya, the hippogryph master outside the north gate
S Everlook @ Winterspring, 61.4, 38.8 | Innkeeper Vizzie, at the inn. Your hearthstone now brings you back here
A 6603 | Meggi Peppinrocker, near the west gate. It goes to Donova on your way back west
A 3783 | Umi Rumplesnicker
A 6604 | Harlo Wigglesworth, next to the inn
A 6028,6030 | Gregor Greystone, in the inn. Both are deliveries to the Plaguelands, at the very end of the route: keep them

# ---------- East of Everlook: yetis and Winterfall Village ----------
C 3783 @ Winterspring, 67.4, 42.3 | Ice Thistle Yetis (55-56) on the hills south-east of Everlook drop the 10 Thick Yeti Furs
C 8464 @ Winterspring, 67.1, 36.8 | Winterfall Village, just east of Everlook: 8 Shamans and 8 Ursa, and whatever Den Watchers Salfa still needs. Only six Shamans live here, so wait for a respawn. The Shamans heal: kill them first and interrupt or stun their casts if your class can. The Ursa (57-58) hit hardest: one at a time, at full health. High Chief Winterfall in the cave at the back (69.6, 38.3) is elite: stay out of it
L 56 @ Winterspring, 67.1, 36.8 | Stay in Winterfall Village and grind to 56 before the higher yetis and the owlbeasts. Pull at the edge of the camp, one at a time; back off from pairs if you can, and eat or bandage between pulls. The yetis next door are an easier alternative
T 3783 | Umi Rumplesnicker, Everlook
A 977 | Umi Rumplesnicker
C 977 @ Winterspring, 69.2, 40.8 | Ice Thistle Matriarchs and Patriarchs (56-58) higher up in the Ice Thistle Hills drop the 2 Pristine Yeti Horns. Pull them one at a time
T 977 | Umi Rumplesnicker. Do not take her third quest: the mechanical yeti has to visit Gadgetzan and Un'Goro and come back here, and you leave Winterspring for good today

# ---------- Lake Kel'Theril and the south ----------
T 6604 | Ride west to Jaron Stoneshaper, Starfall Village
A 4861 | Jaron Stoneshaper
C 5245 @ Winterspring, 53.0, 42.4 | Lake Kel'Theril, south of Starfall. Four Highborne Relic Fragments stick out of the ice (50.9, 41.7; 52.4, 41.5; 53.3, 43.4; 55.1, 43.0): use Jaron's Pick next to each one, then loot it. The Anguished and Suffering Highborne (54-55) around them are ghosts with a mana burn: interrupt it if your class can, otherwise kill them fast. Keep the four fragments for the Plaguelands
T 4861 @ Winterspring, 59.0, 59.8 | Ride south along the road, past the Mazthoril cave (stay on the road), to Jaron's wrecked camp at the edge of Owl Wing Thicket: the Damaged Crate
A 4863 @ Winterspring, 59.0, 59.8 | The Damaged Crate
T 4863 @ Winterspring, 61.4, 60.7 | Jaron's Wagon, a little further east
A 4864 @ Winterspring, 61.4, 60.7 | Jaron's Wagon
C 4864 @ Winterspring, 64.8, 60.8 | Pick up Jaron's Supplies from the snow beside the wagon, then kill Crazed, Moontouched and Berserk Owlbeasts (56-59) around the camp and in Owl Wing Thicket just east until one drops the Blue-feathered Amulet. They hit hard and enrage: one at a time, walk away if a second comes, and heal or bandage early
C 4842 @ Winterspring, 59.8, 74.3 | Ride to the far south until the sky turns dark at the mouth of Darkwhisper Gorge. The way runs through Frostwhisper Gorge (around 58-66, 65-73), whose Frostmaul Giants and Preservers are elite, level 59-60: stay mounted, keep to the middle and do not stop. Reaching the mouth of Darkwhisper Gorge is enough; the demons further in are elite too
T 4864 | Ride back north, through Frostwhisper Gorge the same way, to Jaron Stoneshaper at Starfall Village

# ---------- Back west: Donova and Salfa ----------
T 6603 | Ride west along the road to Donova Snowden at the hot springs
A 5082 | Donova Snowden
T 4842 | Donova Snowden
C 5082 @ Winterspring, 31.8, 36.5 | The two western Winterfall camps again: 8 Pathfinders, 8 Totemics and 8 Den Watchers. Only four Den Watchers live in the west (three in the camp south-east of Salfa at 30.5, 36.3, one in the camp east of Donova at 41.6, 42.6): kill them, do the Pathfinders and Totemics, and they are back for the second round
T 5082 | Donova Snowden
T 8464 | Salfa, at the tunnel exit. Hand him any Winterfall Spirit Beads too, 5 at a time
H Everlook | Use your Hearthstone
N Segment done. Next segment flies south from Everlook | Keep Troubled Spirits of Kel'Theril (5245, with the four relic fragments), The Everlook Report (6028) and Duke Nicholas Zverenhoff (6030) in the log: all three are for the Plaguelands. Sell and repair here; your hearthstone is set to Everlook
